# vis kind=w act=ex_show e="money bag" title="WHAT IS MONEY?" pause=1.2 l="MONEY" around="coin|banknote with dollar sign|credit card"
What if money disappeared tomorrow?
Not just cash. Every number in every account.

# vis kind=w act=ex_compare e="cow|bread" l="A COW|SOME BREAD" sign="≠" title="BARTER"
A cow for some bread?
Hard to split a cow.

# vis kind=w act=ex_flow e="tractor|bread|convenience store|shopping trolley" l="FARM|BAKERY|SHOP|YOU" title="HOW PRICES TRAVEL" bg=sky
The farmer grows the wheat.
The baker bakes it.
The shop sells it.
And you buy it.

# vis kind=w act=ex_stat v=2000 unit="unemployed people, Finland 2017–18" e="bust in silhouette" gn=100 title="THE FINNISH TRIAL" bg=mint
Two thousand people got money every month for two years.

# vis kind=w act=ex_chapter n=2 title="THE QUEUE" sub="when free means waiting" e="hourglass with flowing sand"
Part two. The queue.

# vis kind=w act=ex_list e="busts in silhouette|ticket|scales" l="The queue decides who gets things|A ration card decides how much|Someone writes the rules" title="WHERE MONEY'S JOB GOES" n=1 bg=blush
First, the queue.
Then the card.
Then whoever writes the rules.

# vis kind=w act=ex_quote q="No example of a|barter economy,|pure and simple,|has ever been described." by="Caroline Humphrey, 1985" bg=paper
